# Armarium environment
# Copy to .env.local (Next) / .env (scripts) and fill in.
#
# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  ⚠️  AUTH FOOTGUN — READ THIS FIRST                                                            │
# │                                                                                                │
# │  Omitting the two NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* vars below runs Armarium in NO-AUTH PASSTHROUGH mode  │
# │  (a single shared user, no login gate). That is correct for local dev / CI / the hermetic      │
# │  build — but NEVER deploy publicly without them. A public deploy missing those two vars is a   │
# │  PUBLIC, AUTH-DISABLED app: every visitor shares one closet. isAuthConfigured() (src/lib/      │
# │  auth.ts) keys auth ON/OFF purely on the PRESENCE of both vars.                                 │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# ── Postgres on Supabase (Drizzle) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for db:migrate / db:seed and runtime DB access. When unset the app uses the in-memory repo.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/postgres

# ── Anthropic — SERVER ONLY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required to run the real classification pipeline / seed. Never expose to the client.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxx
# Optional override of the API base URL.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# ── Supabase Auth (Phase 3 — real multi-user) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set BOTH of these to enable real auth + per-user isolation (RLS). They are PUBLIC by design
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_*, inlined into the client bundle at BUILD time — set them before `next build`).
# Leaving EITHER unset = NO-AUTH passthrough mode (see the warning box above). For a public deploy,
# both are REQUIRED.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Supabase SERVICE-ROLE key — SERVER ONLY, never NEXT_PUBLIC, never the client bundle. Grants
# elevated, RLS-bypassing access used for privileged server-side operations: signing private
# item-image storage URLs and account deletion. Required only when those features are active.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# ── v0 one-password gate (NOT real auth) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The legacy password gate, still in place until real auth is fully rolled out.
APP_PASSWORD=changeme
# The single fixed user id used for all passthrough-mode rows.
ARMARIUM_USER_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

# ── Upstash Redis — OPTIONAL (deploy activation) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables a TRUE cross-instance rate-limit ceiling (and the per-IP signup throttle) backed by Redis
# instead of the per-instance in-memory limiter. Set BOTH vars AND run
# `pnpm add @upstash/ratelimit @upstash/redis` on that deploy. When absent (or the packages aren't
# installed), the limiter degrades gracefully to the in-memory token bucket — no behavior change.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=xxxx

# ── Deploy activation note ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres full-text/trigram SEARCH requires migration 0010 to be applied (pnpm db:migrate, or the
# Supabase Management API path in-sandbox). Until then the search path falls back gracefully.
